AKAC Attribution License 1.0-draft
Release date: 2026-09-28
SPDX-style identifier: LicenseRef-AKAC-Attribution-1.0-draft

This custom license is an operative permission for the Covered Material supplied
under it, although the text is a draft and has not received independent legal
review. It is not the Apache License and no OSI approval is represented.

1. Definitions

"Licensor" means a person or entity entitled to license its contribution.
"Covered Material" means the copyrightable software, schemas, policies, tests,
examples or other material expressly designated as subject to this license.
"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this license.
"Modified Material" means modifications or derivative works of Covered Material.
"Hosted Service" means a service through which users interact with Covered
Material or Modified Material over a network without receiving a software copy.
"Required Attribution" means the applicable copyright and authorship notices,
the name AKAC — Agent Knowledge Access Control, and the supplied project-origin
notice identifying Ömer Hüseyin Coşkun as project founder, together with the
project URL https://github.com/WestMoneyDE/AKAC and this license's identity.

2. Permission

Subject to these conditions, each Licensor grants You a worldwide, nonexclusive,
no-charge, royalty-free copyright license to use, reproduce, run, modify, prepare
derivative works, display, perform and distribute its Covered Material, including
commercial use and operation of Hosted Services. You may combine it with other
software, including proprietary software. No source-disclosure, advertising,
payment, telemetry or registration obligation is imposed by this license.

3. Attribution

a. When distributing Covered Material or Modified Material, include a copy of
this license and retain relevant supplied notices. Provide the Required
Attribution in a reasonably accessible credits, legal-notices or documentation
location. A bundled NOTICE or third-party-notices file is sufficient. Do not
require recipients to inspect source code to find notices for a binary product.

b. When operating a Hosted Service using Covered Material or Modified Material,
make the Required Attribution reasonably accessible to that service's users in
credits, legal notices or service documentation. An API-only service may use its
API documentation. A home-page banner, logo or attribution on every response is
not required. For an exclusively internal service, internal documentation or
an internal third-party-notices inventory accessible to its administrators is
sufficient. For solely personal local use, retaining the supplied notices is
sufficient.

c. Identify material modifications and their author in a changelog or other
reasonable notice. Do not falsely attribute modifications to the project founder
or suggest that a Licensor endorses You or your product. The historical project-
origin notice may be retained without claiming that the founder authored all
subsequent contributions.

d. A notice may be adapted in formatting or translated without changing its
substance. It may link to a maintained legal-notices page when appropriate for
the medium. A defunct project URL may be reproduced as an historical identifier.

4. Patent permission

Each Licensor grants a worldwide, nonexclusive, no-charge, royalty-free patent
license to make, use, offer for sale, sell and import Covered Material, limited
to patent claims it can license that are necessarily infringed by its contribution
alone or in combination with the Covered Material to which it was contributed.
No unrelated patent claim is licensed. If You initiate patent litigation alleging
that Covered Material infringes a patent, patent permissions granted to You under
this section terminate as of that filing. This section creates no patent rights
where none exist and does not represent that any patent has been applied for.

5. Downstream rights and contributions

Recipients receive permission under this license directly from the applicable
Licensors. You may license your original modifications under additional terms,
but may not remove permissions and notices applicable to existing Covered
Material. No contributor transfers ownership merely by contributing. Intentional
contributions accepted into this project must be offered under the applicable
file license; the project's contribution process records that confirmation.
Third-party components remain under their own licenses and notices.

6. Names, ideas and independent implementations

No trademark license is granted beyond reasonable identification of origin.
No endorsement or certification is implied. This license does not claim ownership
of abstract ideas, access-control models, public standards or independently
implemented behavior. It imposes no attribution obligation on an independent
implementation merely because it follows an unprotected idea or interface.
The obligations attach only to exercise of rights in the Covered Material.

7. Termination and cure

Permission terminates for a material breach of these conditions. If You cure
the breach within 30 days after receiving written notice identifying it, copyright
permission is automatically reinstated, unless the same breach was previously
notified and cured. A Licensor may expressly reinstate permission in other cases.
Compliant recipients' rights are not terminated by another person's breach.
Except as stated here and in the patent section, permissions are irrevocable
for compliant use of the version received.

